WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.431
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:15.124
Unit three: First Conditional. Today you will talk about real possibilities in the future.

4
00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:17.879
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.171
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:23.635
If.

7
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.975
If means a word that begins a condition.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.235
If it rains, we stay.

9
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.759
Your turn. Say: If.

10
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.241
If.

11
00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:36.648
Will.

12
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.033
Will means the word for a future result.

13
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.838
I will call you.

14
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.800
Your turn. Say: Will.

15
00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.447
Will.

16
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:50.614
Real possibility.

17
00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:55.126
Real possibility means something that may actually happen.

18
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:57.600
Rain is a real possibility.

19
00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:01.380
Your turn. Say: Real possibility.

20
00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:05.827
Real possibility.

21
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:07.642
Condition.

22
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.172
Condition means the thing that must happen first.

23
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.342
Good weather is the condition.

24
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.138
Your turn. Say: Condition.

25
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.106
Condition.

26
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:21.921
Result.

27
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:25.648
Result means what happens because of the condition.

28
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.913
The result was positive.

29
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:31.436
Your turn. Say: Result.

30
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.429
Result.

31
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:37.126
Likely.

32
00:01:38.117 --> 00:01:39.652
Likely means probable.

33
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.855
Rain is likely tomorrow.

34
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.684
Your turn. Say: Likely.

35
00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:48.372
Likely.

36
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:50.454
Future outcome.

37
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.902
Future outcome means what will happen later.

38
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:56.168
The outcome depends on you.

39
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.842
Your turn. Say: Future outcome.

40
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.235
Future outcome.

41
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:05.613
Rule.

42
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:10.079
Rule means a statement that explains how grammar works.

43
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:12.114
The rule is simple.

44
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:15.636
Your turn. Say: Rule.

45
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.513
Rule.

46
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.637
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:29.153
Visal, complete this: If I have free time this weekend, I will…

48
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:42.481
If I have free time this weekend, I will visit my grandmother. The first conditional is for real or likely future situations: if + present simple, will + base verb.

49
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:45.165
Why not use will after if?

50
00:02:46.250 --> 00:03:00.341
Because the if-clause is the condition, and we use the present simple for it. We say if it rains, not if it will rain. The result clause uses will, can, might or an imperative.

51
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.846
Can we change the order?

52
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:16.174
Yes. We will stay at home if it rains. When the if-clause comes second, there is no comma. We can also use unless, which means if not: Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.

53
00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:19.217
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:26.019
Grammar focus: First conditional: If plus present simple, will plus base verb.

55
00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:27.517
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:31.412
If I have free time, I will visit my grandmother.

57
00:03:32.317 --> 00:03:34.386
If it rains, we will stay at home.

58
00:03:35.283 --> 00:03:37.492
Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.

59
00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:47.276
Use if + present simple, will + base verb for real future possibilities. Do not put will in the if-clause. Unless means if not.

60
00:03:48.017 --> 00:03:51.400
Be careful! Don't say: If it will rain, we stay home.

61
00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.982
Say: If it rains, we will stay home.

62
00:03:56.282 --> 00:03:58.293
Use the present simple after if.

63
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.683
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:03.770
If This, Then That.

65
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.509
If I have free time this weekend, I will visit my grandmother.

66
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.592
If it rains, we will stay at home.

67
00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.994
Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.

68
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.928
If you study hard, you will probably pass.

69
00:04:18.933 --> 00:04:22.361
These are real possibilities, so the outcome is likely.

70
00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:27.352
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:28.217 --> 00:04:30.820
If it blank tomorrow, we will stay home.

72
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.622
A, will rain. B, rains. C, rained.

73
00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.108
The answer is B: rains.

74
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.215
If I see him, I blank him.

75
00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:46.681
A, tell. B, will tell. C, told.

76
00:04:50.233 --> 00:04:52.186
The answer is B: will tell.

77
00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.908
'Unless' means blank.

78
00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:58.455
A, if not. B, because. C, when.

79
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.510
The answer is A: if not.

80
00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.139
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:13.275
A, If you will come, I will wait.. B, If you come, I will wait.. C, If you came, I will wait..

82
00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.390
The answer is B: If you come, I will wait..

83
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.444
According to the reading, what are these situations?

84
00:05:23.744 --> 00:05:28.442
A, real possibilities. B, dreams. C, past events.

85
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.986
The answer is A: real possibilities.

86
00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.433
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:40.283 --> 00:05:44.303
Complete this sentence: If I have free time this weekend, I will...

88
00:05:53.117 --> 00:05:54.594
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:54.894 --> 00:06:07.626
If I have free time this weekend, I will visit my grandmother and help her in the garden. If the weather is good, we will have lunch outside. I use the present simple in the if-clause and will in the result.

90
00:06:07.926 --> 00:06:09.635
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:17.997
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and first conditional: if plus present simple, will plus base verb.

92
00:06:18.297 --> 00:06:22.935
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:23.235 --> 00:06:25.725
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:26.025 --> 00:06:28.700
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

